# Node scripts must keep LF line endings: a CRLF shebang breaks tooling that
# executes the file through a VM (the vitest/Vite SSR transform), so tests
# that import these scripts fail on Windows checkouts (core.autocrlf=true).
*.mjs text eol=lf

# Rust sources and TOML manifests must keep LF on disk as well. On Windows
# checkouts (core.autocrlf=true) they otherwise land as CRLF, while cargo,
# tauri dev and rust-analyzer rewrite them with LF (observed:
# client/src-tauri/Cargo.toml was the only LF TOML in a CRLF checkout). Each
# rewrite changes the file size and mtime without changing the normalized
# content, so the index stat cache goes stale and `git status` reports the
# file as modified while `git diff` is empty.
*.toml text eol=lf
*.rs text eol=lf
